  <title>Interpret the Growth Factor of the Equation</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01307</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Interpret the Growth Factor of the Equation</md:title>
    <md:uuid>45e22392-e73a-420f-b7f5-059f42fc8f02</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down</title>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00001" class="unnumbered">
  <problem id="prob-00001">
    <para id="para-00001">A group of biologists is surveying the mice population in a forest. The equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>75</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> gives the total number of mice, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> years since the survey began. Explain what the numbers 75 and 3 mean in this situation.</para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00001">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00002">Compare your answer: </para>
    
    <para id="para-00003">75 is the initial number of mice in the forest when the survey started, or the number of mice when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 0. The 3 is the growth factor or constant ratio, meaning that each year, the population of mice in the forest is 3 times the previous year’s population.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
</content>
